From 35c889e2a1642ee5992be938c2a20115f5e48c46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini PDA experiment <experiment.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:40:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] workqueue: name a null pool after WLAN START

The first START was followed by a delayed-work NULL pool panic. Print
the workqueue name and work function if that fault recurs, then leave
the existing fatal behavior unchanged for private pstore recovery.

Internal diagnostic only; synthetic non-certifying author, no DCO.
---
 kernel/workqueue.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/workqueue.c b/kernel/workqueue.c
index 33b721a..25558c7 100644
--- a/kernel/workqueue.c
+++ b/kernel/workqueue.c
@@ -2322,6 +2322,9 @@ retry:
 
 	pwq = rcu_dereference(*per_cpu_ptr(wq->cpu_pwq, cpu));
 	pool = pwq->pool;
+	if (unlikely(!pool))
+		pr_emerg("Gemini WLAN diagnostic: null workqueue pool wq=%s work=%ps cpu=%d\n",
+			 wq->name, work->func, cpu);
 
 	/*
 	 * If @work was previously on a different pool, it might still be
